# Consumed on Linux; routinely cloned on Windows, where git's default
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites text files on checkout and breaks things quietly:
# a CRLF shebang makes a script "no such file or directory", and a field match
# against "value\r" silently fails. Both have already cost this project time -
# see a50-halium's .gitattributes commit. Force LF.
* text=auto eol=lf
deviceinfo text eol=lf
build.sh text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.rules text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
*.sha256 text eol=lf
ramdisk-overlay/** text eol=lf
overlay/** text eol=lf

*.img binary
*.gz binary
*.xz binary
